Every file here is the release's own, byte for byte. Nothing is edited, added
to, or patched.

Vendored: src/core, src/include and src/netif, which is what netd compiles and
the headers those sources include. src/api and src/apps are not here because
nothing builds them.

Adaptations are outside this tree, so an update is a re-fetch rather than a
merge:

  src/user/netd/lwipport/lwipopts.h    configuration
  src/user/netd/lwipport/arch/cc.h     compiler and platform hooks
  src/user/netd/lwip.zig               the Zig mirror and the C-calls-Zig
                                       boundary; lwipport/layout_check.c pins
                                       the struct offsets it relies on

To update: fetch a release, replace the three directories with the release's
own, then build netd. layout_check.c fails the build if a struct the mirror
uses has moved.
